<title> Acute Interstitial Nephritis. </title>
<graphic href="eee0637-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Patient with acute renal failure and suspected acute interstitial nephritis</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Stop all potential offending medications, monitor renal function and clinical status over 4-7 days</label>
<path target="cell-3">BUN/Cr recovers</path>
<path target="cell-4">No improvement or worsening of BUN/Cr</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-3">
<label>Continue supportive care, and document hypersensitivity reaction</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Obtain renal biopsy</label>
<path target="cell-7">Diagnosis of AIN</path>
<path target="cell-5">Other diagnosis</path>
<path target="cell-6">Patient refusal or unstable</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Treat alternate diagnosis</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Consider gallium scan and&#x002F;or empiric treatment</label>
<path target="cell-8"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Start prednisone at 1 mg&#x002F;kg&#x002F;day</label>
<path target="cell-8">BUN/Cr recovers</path>
<path target="cell-9">No improvement or worsening of BUN/Cr</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Continue at same dose for 1-2 weeks, then taper over 4-8 weeks</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Consider alternative immunosuppressive medications (eg, cyclophosphamides)</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
